  {
    "episode_id": 91236,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91236.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 159,
    "turn_text": "I want to talk a little bit about what your strategy would be if you were in the general election, if you were the nominee as opposed to the other candidates. A lot of the candidates, both in the last race and in this year already, have fallen into the trap when they're campaigning against Donald Trump of trading insults with him. getting into this endless cycle of barbs and the media loves to cover that stuff. Correct me if I'm wrong. I feel like you have a little bit of a different strategy. You don't seem to want to engage Trump on that level. You always seem to want to continue talking to voters almost past him at all times, just focus on the issues, focus on your message of corporate power. If you were the nominee, how would you deal with Donald Trump differently from the other candidates?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
